 "drivingQuestion": "If no one else betrothed her within the thirty days, is she betrothed?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "Rav and Shmuel rule she is betrothed",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "kiddushin.59a.9",
   "daf": "59a",
   "sentenceId": 8,
   "he": "וְכֵן הָאוֹמֵר לְאִשָּׁה הִתְקַדְּשִׁי לִי כּוּ׳. לֹא בָּא אַחֵר וְקִידְּשָׁה בְּתוֹךְ שְׁלֹשִׁים, מַהוּ? רַב וּשְׁמוּאֵל דְּאָמְרִי תַּרְוַיְיהוּ: מְקוּדֶּשֶׁת, וְאַף עַל פִּי שֶׁנִּתְאַכְּלוּ הַמָּעוֹת.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «And similarly,» with regard to «one who says to a woman: Be betrothed to me» after thirty days, and another came and betrothed her within this period, she is betrothed to the second man. The Gemara asks: In a case where «another did not come and betroth her within» the «thirty» days, «what is» the halakha? «Rav and Shmuel both say: She is betrothed» after thirty days, «even if the money» he gave for her betrothal «has been used» before the end of this period, as the betrothal takes effect from when the money is given."
  }
 ],
